        }
      ],
      "extract": "In this section, we recall a basic theory of *Gröbner-Shirshov bases* for associative algebras to make the paper self-contained. \\ Let $X$ be a set and let $\\langle X\\rangle$ be the free monoid of associative words on $X$. We denote the empty word by $1$ and the *length* (or *degree*) of a word $u$ by $l(u)$. A well-ordering $<$ on $\\langle X\\rangle$ is called a *monomial order* if $x<y$ implies $axb<ayb$ for all",
      "extractCut": true
