          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "The Coxeter group of type $H_2=I_2(5)$ is just the dihedral group of a regular pentagon. That is the group generated by two reflections $s_1, s_2$ with relation $$(s_1s_2)^5=1.$$ If we let $G$ be the Coxeter group of type $H_2$ and take the complex field $\\mathbb{C}$ as our base field, then the group algebra $\\mathbb{C}[G]$ is generated by $s_1,s_2$ with the defining relations $$s_1^2=1=s_2^2,\\quad",
      "extractCut": true
    },
